          "author": "@JayRuks-b4d",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/6Z7ebUFnbizjQkR3b40i13qGuawcRPcqcTMQ18HMyvGz2wQOYmRahWHky67sbzL867rHqjmlaA=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "​​​@BenNtabangiraYou must be slow dear.. I know the language is Kinyawanda...I speak it.. Murakoze...but even your own people use Kinyi as a slang.. cause who wants to write the whole Kinyarwanda term...get with the program please...before you try to educate me...because you can't!!!Murakoze cyane!Mbye-Mbye🙋🏽‍♀😂",
          "likeCount": 0,
          "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T17:27:49Z"
        },
        {
          "id": "UgxShvajP7fV4Y9Fgk94AaABAg.AcCAW4i9Oc3Ad4Wbe8PLqa",
          "author": "@JayRuks-b4d",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/6Z7ebUFnbizjQkR3b40i13qGuawcRPcqcTMQ18HMyvGz2wQOYmRahWHky67sbzL867rHqjmlaA=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "​@AzanConceptsYou must be mistaken or talking about a different Rwanda...1st of all which people are you refering to?The locals?Do you know how many locals and even the poorer of the poorest in Rwanda own land?esp. agriculture?and 2ndly...anyone can buy land in Rwanda...even if you're a foreigner and not even living in Rwanda...do your research properly please...all you need is money and a good damn brain and a lot of research...any more questions, do not hesitate!🤷🏾‍♀",
